1
00:00:50,550 --> 00:00:51,760
How many more people
will have to experience

2
00:00:51,843 --> 00:00:53,553
the same pain we went through, Alex?

3
00:00:53,636 --> 00:00:54,637
Enough, Alex.

4
00:00:54,721 --> 00:00:55,764
It's already too painful.

5
00:01:02,520 --> 00:01:07,692
Or maybe Mikoy is the key
to bring down the whole agency.

6
00:01:14,157 --> 00:01:15,784
You are the person that has been
with Chiara the longest.

7
00:01:15,867 --> 00:01:17,952
<i>You're the only trainee she had.</i>

8
00:01:18,036 --> 00:01:20,830
<i>And you are the only person who knows her.</i>

9
00:01:24,709 --> 00:01:26,419
We both know that when the two of you
are facing each other,

10
00:01:26,503 --> 00:01:28,046
you'll be needing that kind of courage.

11
00:01:35,970 --> 00:01:36,971
What will you do, Chiara?

12
00:01:37,055 --> 00:01:38,681
Kill everyone who refuses to follow you?

13
00:01:38,765 --> 00:01:40,850
Of course not. That would be exhausting.

14
00:02:02,330 --> 00:02:03,248
So,

15
00:02:03,998 --> 00:02:05,041
it's confirmed?

16
00:02:19,097 --> 00:02:20,265
It's not that simple.

17
00:02:21,015 --> 00:02:23,143
Prague is Valtrovi territory.

18
00:02:23,935 --> 00:02:26,855
That's where their family is strongest,
and they have people everywhere.

19
00:02:29,732 --> 00:02:32,610
Yup, and now that she's leading
the Concordat,

20
00:02:32,694 --> 00:02:35,196
her network has expanded even further.

21
00:02:42,245 --> 00:02:43,830
Then we find a way she won't know about.

22
00:02:43,913 --> 00:02:45,039
Mikoy.

23
00:02:45,665 --> 00:02:47,584
We found her, didn't we?

24
00:02:47,667 --> 00:02:48,501
It's confirmed.

25
00:02:49,168 --> 00:02:50,378
What are we waiting for?

26
00:02:50,461 --> 00:02:52,714
A chance that we won't all die.

27
00:02:56,801 --> 00:02:57,635
So that's it?

28
00:02:58,386 --> 00:02:59,596
What do you mean by that?

29
00:02:59,679 --> 00:03:01,306
We found the person, didn't we?

30
00:03:01,806 --> 00:03:02,682
And we're not going to do anything?

31
00:03:03,808 --> 00:03:05,852
I'm not saying
we're not going to do anything.

32
00:03:17,864 --> 00:03:18,865
What about us?

33
00:03:20,325 --> 00:03:21,701
What about all of us?

34
00:03:22,952 --> 00:03:24,120
Are you the only one going?

35
00:03:25,955 --> 00:03:28,541
Because the moment
you authorize an operation,

36
00:03:28,625 --> 00:03:31,044
the whole agency is involved.

37
00:03:31,836 --> 00:03:33,254
I'm not forcing you to come.

38
00:03:37,300 --> 00:03:39,844
You're not thinking
like part of the team anymore.

39
00:03:39,928 --> 00:03:41,930
All you care about is getting to Chiara.

40
00:03:42,013 --> 00:03:43,306
Of all of us here,

41
00:03:43,389 --> 00:03:45,600
I have the biggest reason to get to her,

42
00:03:45,683 --> 00:03:46,559
and you know that.

43
00:03:53,608 --> 00:03:54,734
What do you mean?

44
00:03:55,652 --> 00:03:56,861
Mikoy, you've lost someone.

45
00:03:57,612 --> 00:03:59,948
You're hurting. You're angry.

46
00:04:00,031 --> 00:04:01,282
And right now,

47
00:04:01,366 --> 00:04:03,576
you're letting your grief
make the decisions for you.

48
00:04:03,660 --> 00:04:05,078
There you go again.

49
00:04:05,161 --> 00:04:06,871
You don't know how I feel.

50
00:04:08,665 --> 00:04:10,667
Then stop using your concern as an excuse

51
00:04:10,750 --> 00:04:12,335
for us to do nothing.

52
00:04:12,418 --> 00:04:14,087
Because I don't want
anything bad to happen to you.

53
00:04:14,170 --> 00:04:16,005
Did I ask you to worry about me?

54
00:04:17,882 --> 00:04:19,884
Mikoy, this isn't about
what you're asking for.

55
00:04:21,344 --> 00:04:24,806
It's my job to make sure
the people with me make it home safely.

56
00:04:24,889 --> 00:04:27,642
And it's our job to go after criminals.

57
00:04:28,226 --> 00:04:29,185
Right?

58
00:04:31,729 --> 00:04:32,563
There she is.

59
00:04:34,023 --> 00:04:35,566
What are we waiting for?

60
00:04:54,460 --> 00:04:56,337
- Mikoy.
- Mikoy!

61
00:05:14,063 --> 00:05:14,939
Mikoy.

62
00:05:15,565 --> 00:05:16,566
Mikoy.

63
00:05:23,740 --> 00:05:25,658
I know I'm not your father.

64
00:05:27,201 --> 00:05:30,288
And I have no intention
of replacing Mario in your life.

65
00:05:31,789 --> 00:05:33,958
But I've known you for a long time.

66
00:05:34,042 --> 00:05:36,919
I've seen you scared.

67
00:05:37,420 --> 00:05:39,338
I've seen you

68
00:05:41,174 --> 00:05:42,508
make mistakes.

69
00:05:42,592 --> 00:05:44,177
I've seen you fight.

70
00:05:45,511 --> 00:05:47,889
And after all this time
you've been with this agency,

71
00:05:47,972 --> 00:05:50,683
I've come to see you as my own son.

72
00:05:59,275 --> 00:06:05,156
That's why I can't just stand here
and watch you like this.

73
00:06:07,700 --> 00:06:08,993
I'm okay, sir.

74
00:06:12,205 --> 00:06:14,582
I'm looking for justice for my father.

75
00:06:21,798 --> 00:06:22,882
Bok.

76
00:06:24,550 --> 00:06:25,927
Are you okay?

77
00:06:28,262 --> 00:06:29,222
I'm okay.

78
00:06:32,558 --> 00:06:33,643
But him?

79
00:06:33,726 --> 00:06:34,644
He doesn't look okay.

80
00:06:36,562 --> 00:06:38,147
He's just angry.

81
00:06:38,231 --> 00:06:39,690
Bok, it's not just anger.

82
00:06:40,525 --> 00:06:42,151
I don't know if you've noticed.

83
00:06:43,027 --> 00:06:43,861
What?

84
00:06:44,570 --> 00:06:45,446
Bok.

85
00:06:45,530 --> 00:06:47,156
Mikoy has changed.

86
00:06:47,657 --> 00:06:50,118
He's not the Mikoy
we've known all these years.

87
00:06:51,410 --> 00:06:52,578
He doesn't stop training.

88
00:06:52,662 --> 00:06:55,331
And he barely sleeps anymore.

89
00:06:56,916 --> 00:06:58,835
His father just died.

90
00:07:00,211 --> 00:07:02,296
That's why I'm worried, Bok.

91
00:07:04,465 --> 00:07:05,842
He's still grieving.

92
00:07:05,925 --> 00:07:07,176
That doesn't mean that--

93
00:07:07,260 --> 00:07:09,595
Exactly. That's why I'm worried.

94
00:07:12,807 --> 00:07:14,350
What do you mean?

95
00:07:15,726 --> 00:07:18,354
Bok, I don't know if you've noticed…

96
00:07:21,607 --> 00:07:22,608
Bok.

97
00:07:23,776 --> 00:07:25,069
Justice?

98
00:07:27,572 --> 00:07:31,325
Or are you looking for someone
to take your anger out on?

99
00:07:31,409 --> 00:07:33,619
We already know who killed him.

100
00:07:35,246 --> 00:07:36,956
So what's the problem?

101
00:07:37,039 --> 00:07:38,583
The problem is…

102
00:07:41,043 --> 00:07:43,671
my conscience won't let me,

103
00:07:43,754 --> 00:07:46,257
when Mario and I meet again,

104
00:07:46,340 --> 00:07:50,803
just stand by and let his son
follow him right away.

105
00:07:50,887 --> 00:07:53,598
That's not the justice he wanted.

106
00:07:55,475 --> 00:07:57,935
Dad is gone. He can't tell us
what he wants anymore.

107
00:08:01,814 --> 00:08:03,774
So don't use his name

108
00:08:03,858 --> 00:08:09,989
to justify something that you want to do.

109
00:08:14,744 --> 00:08:15,828
Bro.

110
00:08:23,169 --> 00:08:24,295
What are you doing here?

111
00:08:27,298 --> 00:08:28,841
Can we talk?

112
00:08:32,220 --> 00:08:34,096
Go, talk to each other.

113
00:08:53,824 --> 00:08:55,785
Even though he knows
it could get him killed.

114
00:08:57,078 --> 00:08:58,746
I won't let that happen.

115
00:09:06,754 --> 00:09:09,215
Because I think
Mikoy's biggest enemy right now

116
00:09:09,298 --> 00:09:10,383
is no one else

117
00:09:11,425 --> 00:09:13,135
but himself.

118
00:09:38,911 --> 00:09:39,787
Mom?

119
00:09:40,329 --> 00:09:41,539
How is she?

120
00:09:43,541 --> 00:09:44,750
She's okay.

121
00:09:45,960 --> 00:09:47,295
Or so she says.

122
00:09:52,717 --> 00:09:53,634
What about you?

123
00:09:55,928 --> 00:09:56,971
I'm okay too.

124
00:09:59,015 --> 00:10:00,016
Or so you say?

125
00:10:01,517 --> 00:10:02,685
Guess it runs in the family.

126
00:10:08,649 --> 00:10:09,817
Bro.

127
00:10:11,485 --> 00:10:13,529
We don't really get to talk anymore.

128
00:10:15,156 --> 00:10:16,574
But we're talking right now.

129
00:10:18,993 --> 00:10:20,911
What I mean is,

130
00:10:21,621 --> 00:10:24,707
ever since Dad passed away,

131
00:10:26,167 --> 00:10:29,253
it feels like we've all had
our own things going on.

132
00:10:31,589 --> 00:10:34,508
Mom's been busy taking care of us,

133
00:10:35,760 --> 00:10:37,470
and I've been looking after Mom.

134
00:10:40,431 --> 00:10:41,265
And you?

135
00:10:42,808 --> 00:10:45,102
I don't know even know
what you've been up to, bro.

136
00:10:48,397 --> 00:10:50,107
I just have something
I need to take care of.

137
00:10:52,777 --> 00:10:53,903
For Dad?

138
00:10:59,825 --> 00:11:01,160
For Dad.

139
00:11:07,333 --> 00:11:08,751
I really miss him so much, bro.

140
00:11:10,294 --> 00:11:12,004
Sometimes I even forget.

141
00:11:13,672 --> 00:11:14,965
When I wake up,

142
00:11:15,758 --> 00:11:17,468
I think everything's still normal.

143
00:11:17,551 --> 00:11:18,677
Then,

144
00:11:19,637 --> 00:11:21,013
I look for him,

145
00:11:21,097 --> 00:11:22,973
wanting to talk to him.

146
00:11:24,308 --> 00:11:26,143
And then I remember…

147
00:11:29,647 --> 00:11:30,856
he's gone.

148
00:11:39,532 --> 00:11:40,616
What about you?

149
00:11:41,534 --> 00:11:42,993
Do you miss Dad?

150
00:11:47,123 --> 00:11:48,332
Every day.

151
00:11:54,380 --> 00:11:55,714
But I have to stay strong.

152
00:11:59,093 --> 00:12:01,679
Bro, you don't have
to be strong around me.

153
00:12:02,179 --> 00:12:03,556
I'm your brother.

154
00:12:11,480 --> 00:12:13,315
I'm so angry, Angelito.

155
00:12:17,862 --> 00:12:20,239
I didn't even get to say a proper goodbye.

156
00:12:23,534 --> 00:12:25,369
There was still so much
I wanted to tell him…

157
00:12:28,080 --> 00:12:29,957
and so much I wanted to do with him.

158
00:12:40,259 --> 00:12:41,218
Me too, bro.

159
00:12:55,065 --> 00:12:55,900
Bro.

160
00:12:56,692 --> 00:12:58,527
Please, don't leave me too.

161
00:13:32,895 --> 00:13:34,605
So what's the plan?

162
00:13:42,947 --> 00:13:44,907
I've already talked to Alex.

163
00:13:44,990 --> 00:13:47,910
I told her I'm a little worried
about Mikoy

164
00:13:47,993 --> 00:13:50,996
because I don't think
he's thinking clearly anymore.

165
00:13:53,207 --> 00:13:54,750
And she believed you?

166
00:13:56,794 --> 00:13:59,255
I don't need her to believe me.

167
00:13:59,338 --> 00:14:02,591
All I need is to give her
a reason to doubt.

168
00:14:05,970 --> 00:14:07,680
And the best part is,

169
00:14:08,430 --> 00:14:10,432
I don't even have to lie.

170
00:14:11,016 --> 00:14:11,850
Because?

171
00:14:11,934 --> 00:14:15,771
Because Mikoy seems
like a very unstable man,

172
00:14:15,854 --> 00:14:18,399
and anyone who sees him

173
00:14:18,482 --> 00:14:19,650
will believe it.

174
00:14:23,737 --> 00:14:24,780
If he gets killed?

175
00:14:29,326 --> 00:14:31,954
Or he has to do it himself.

176
00:14:32,496 --> 00:14:34,707
It has to be his own doing.

177
00:14:38,502 --> 00:14:39,920
But what about Alex?

178
00:14:42,214 --> 00:14:43,257
When that happens,

179
00:14:44,592 --> 00:14:47,303
that's when she'll think back
to everything I told her.

180
00:15:00,649 --> 00:15:01,692
Hey, hey!

181
00:15:25,049 --> 00:15:28,177
Just make sure there's no evidence.

182
00:15:28,260 --> 00:15:30,054
Nothing that could make anyone suspect

183
00:15:30,137 --> 00:15:32,056
that someone else did it.

184
00:15:32,139 --> 00:15:33,599
A brokenhearted man

185
00:15:34,558 --> 00:15:35,976
and a grieving son

186
00:15:37,019 --> 00:15:38,020
who just couldn't take it anymore.

187
00:15:41,690 --> 00:15:42,524
It's perfect.

188
00:15:43,776 --> 00:15:45,819
They'll all think the same thing.

189
00:15:50,824 --> 00:15:52,534
You can't make a mistake.

190
00:15:53,869 --> 00:15:55,913
Because if Chiara finds out

191
00:15:55,996 --> 00:15:57,957
that we touched Mikoy…

192
00:15:58,040 --> 00:15:59,249
No.

193
00:16:03,337 --> 00:16:04,421
No one will ever know.

194
00:16:06,382 --> 00:16:07,508
End it well.

195
00:16:37,538 --> 00:16:38,831
I don't trust him.

196
00:16:39,999 --> 00:16:41,000
Who?

197
00:16:42,334 --> 00:16:43,252
Sianong.

198
00:16:45,170 --> 00:16:47,047
We've already talked about this.

199
00:16:47,131 --> 00:16:48,882
I still don't trust him.

200
00:16:51,301 --> 00:16:53,429
You're not supposed to trust him.

201
00:16:54,096 --> 00:16:55,180
What about you?

202
00:16:55,264 --> 00:16:56,432
Do you trust him?

203
00:16:58,851 --> 00:16:59,977
Mom, he's a traitor.

204
00:17:01,520 --> 00:17:03,313
If he betrayed GAGO,

205
00:17:03,397 --> 00:17:06,150
what assurance do we have
that he won't do the same to us?

206
00:17:06,984 --> 00:17:10,654
He knows what will happen
to him if he does.

207
00:17:14,199 --> 00:17:15,159
What if that's not enough?

208
00:17:16,994 --> 00:17:17,995
What if he can't do it?

209
00:17:27,546 --> 00:17:28,881
you'll do it.

210
00:18:23,268 --> 00:18:27,147
The mission transfers to you, my dear.

211
00:18:30,275 --> 00:18:32,611
If Sianong can't do it anymore,

212
00:18:33,195 --> 00:18:34,488
you finish it.

213
00:18:36,657 --> 00:18:39,743
That's why I had you trained
your whole life,

214
00:18:39,827 --> 00:18:42,246
to do things like this.

215
00:18:43,330 --> 00:18:44,581
You can handle it.

216
00:19:07,563 --> 00:19:09,273
You want me to kill Brother Mikoy?

217
00:19:09,857 --> 00:19:12,401
I want you to do what you have to do.

218
00:19:12,484 --> 00:19:13,318
But, Mom…

219
00:19:17,906 --> 00:19:19,741
If Sianong fails,

220
00:19:54,109 --> 00:19:55,360
You've been caught like this
so many times,

221
00:19:55,444 --> 00:19:56,904
and you still haven't learned.

222
00:20:04,661 --> 00:20:05,662
You've gotten heavier.

223
00:20:20,677 --> 00:20:21,762
Is that for me?

224
00:20:36,109 --> 00:20:36,985
Sianong.

225
00:20:38,570 --> 00:20:39,613
Bok.

226
00:20:39,696 --> 00:20:40,656
Don't move.

227
00:20:40,739 --> 00:20:42,741
Or I swear I'll shoot you!

228
00:20:43,784 --> 00:20:44,743
So it's true.

229
00:20:45,244 --> 00:20:47,663
There really is a traitor in the agency.

230
00:20:55,045 --> 00:20:55,879
You?

231
00:21:01,593 --> 00:21:03,428
I trusted you.

232
00:21:03,929 --> 00:21:05,973
We trusted you.

233
00:21:07,766 --> 00:21:08,934
Who's giving you orders?

234
00:21:10,477 --> 00:21:12,020
Who are you working for?

235
00:21:14,856 --> 00:21:15,774
The Concordat?

236
00:21:16,775 --> 00:21:17,985
Chiara?

237
00:21:28,120 --> 00:21:28,996
Carlota.

238
00:21:30,163 --> 00:21:31,623
Don't talk to me.

239
00:21:36,962 --> 00:21:38,839
What else is there to explain?

240
00:21:40,799 --> 00:21:42,092
While I was with you,

241
00:21:42,801 --> 00:21:45,137
while I trusted you,

242
00:21:45,846 --> 00:21:47,556
you were just using all of us.

243
00:21:47,639 --> 00:21:49,349
I didn't use you, okay?

244
00:21:49,975 --> 00:21:51,059
No.

245
00:21:52,602 --> 00:21:53,687
You know me.

246
00:21:55,522 --> 00:21:56,690
Carlota.

247
00:21:57,274 --> 00:21:58,984
We're done.

248
00:22:04,072 --> 00:22:04,906
Just like that?

249
00:22:12,122 --> 00:22:14,166
I don't even know what's real anymore.

250
00:22:14,249 --> 00:22:15,083
Us.

251
00:22:15,792 --> 00:22:16,877
We are what's real!

252
00:22:17,836 --> 00:22:19,004
Carlota.

253
00:22:31,349 --> 00:22:33,268
Carlota, compared to anyone else,

254
00:22:33,351 --> 00:22:35,729
you're the one who knows me best.

255
00:22:39,107 --> 00:22:40,734
I love you.

256
00:22:44,196 --> 00:22:45,739
I love you so much.

257
00:22:59,377 --> 00:23:00,378
Don't come any closer.

258
00:23:02,506 --> 00:23:04,591
- I'm going to do it.
- Sianong, that's enough!

259
00:23:09,387 --> 00:23:10,222
Alex.

260
00:23:10,931 --> 00:23:12,057
- Mikoy!
- Mikoy?

261
00:23:12,140 --> 00:23:13,100
Mikoy again?

262
00:23:13,725 --> 00:23:16,603
Mikoy, Mikoy, Mikoy again!

263
00:23:17,145 --> 00:23:19,523
Sianong, let Carlota go.

264
00:23:19,606 --> 00:23:21,483
No one's going to chase you.

265
00:23:28,615 --> 00:23:29,491
Let her go.

266
00:23:59,521 --> 00:24:01,690
- He likes to make plans.
- Sianong?

267
00:24:01,773 --> 00:24:05,110
He even made a list of places
he wanted to visit.

268
00:24:05,193 --> 00:24:06,069
- Wait.
- What?

269
00:24:06,153 --> 00:24:07,320
Italy.

270
00:24:07,404 --> 00:24:09,030
- Castellani.
- What?!

271
00:24:09,114 --> 00:24:10,490
Castellani!

272
00:24:18,081 --> 00:24:19,124
Have you seen Sianong?

273
00:24:19,207 --> 00:24:21,585
Ma'am, we've been here for a while,
and we haven't seen him.

274
00:24:21,668 --> 00:24:23,587
Agent Alex, it's open.
He might come in through here.

275
00:24:23,670 --> 00:24:25,505
Stay here and let us know if you see him.

276
00:24:27,007 --> 00:24:29,134
Ouch!

277
00:24:29,217 --> 00:24:30,051
Easy.

278
00:24:30,135 --> 00:24:31,136
Where's Sianong?

279
00:24:31,219 --> 00:24:32,929
- He's the mole.
- Where is he?

280
00:24:33,013 --> 00:24:33,972
He escaped.

281
00:24:34,055 --> 00:24:34,973
How about Mikoy?

282
00:24:35,056 --> 00:24:36,558
He's with Alex.

283
00:24:36,641 --> 00:24:37,809
They're after him.

284
00:24:40,270 --> 00:24:43,148
- Yes?
- I need help. They're after me.

285
00:24:47,360 --> 00:24:49,112
- And you failed!
- Was that all for nothing?

286
00:24:49,196 --> 00:24:50,530
This is where it ends, Sianong.
